 "meta_notes": {
  "headline": "k2_shortfall_replicates = TRUE. At M2/M3 both K=1 arms saturate under BOTH framings and both K=2 arms miss under BOTH framings, all clearing their floors by >=2 SD. This is the FIRST finding in this line to survive replication -- four earlier walls did not.",
  "confound_resolved": "doc 48 SS11.1 warned the criterion might manufacture K-dependence, since saturating a 1.00 bound demands >=0.94 while saturating 0.75 demands >=0.69. M1 answers it: there the K=2 bound is 1.0000 and S2 reaches 0.9854, W-wide 1.0000 -- K=2 arms DO saturate a 1.0 bound when the task allows. The M2/M3 shortfall is therefore not an artifact of bound level. The two framings also agree on all 12 rows.",
  "disambiguator_not_offered": "doc 48 SS11.3's free disambiguator (a cell with K=1 bound ~0.85-0.95 and K=2 bound 1.00) did NOT occur on this draw: K=1 bounds were 0.7500 (M2) and 0.6875 (M3). Recorded as not-offered.",
  "width_vs_depth": "W-wide - S2 = +0.132 (M2), +0.101 (M3), replicating C's +0.175/+0.118. STILL parameter-confounded (33 vs 15 params/verb, doc 48 SS10.3): at K=2 nothing saturates, so width-vs-capacity remains OPEN and this run was not designed to close it. W-work - S1 = -0.045 (M2), +0.009 (M3): workspace adds nothing.",
